menu "Application Module"

config APP_PROVISION_BUTTON_GPIO
    int "Provision button GPIO"
    default 17
    range -1 48
    help
        GPIO for the physical provision button (active-low, internal pull-up,
        wired to GND on press). The press is event-driven via a GPIO ISR that
        notifies the Application task — the CPU never polls the pin.

        Hold the button for APP_PROVISION_BUTTON_HOLD_MS to arm the
        provisioning window. Set to -1 to disable the button entirely.

config APP_PROVISION_BUTTON_HOLD_MS
    int "Provision button hold duration (ms)"
    default 2000
    range 100 10000
    help
        How long the button must be held before the provisioning window is
        armed. A deliberate hold prevents accidental taps from arming it.
        (Irrelevant when APP_PROVISION_BUTTON_GPIO is -1; kept always-defined
        so the code compiles in the disabled configuration.)

config APP_PROVISION_BUTTON_DEBOUNCE_MS
    int "Provision button debounce (ms)"
    default 30
    range 1 200
    help
        Debounce window applied in task context after the ISR fires.
        (Irrelevant when APP_PROVISION_BUTTON_GPIO is -1; kept always-defined
        so the code compiles in the disabled configuration.)

endmenu
